the  character falls deeper into his lie  becoming a worse person for it a flat  character arc therefore belongs to one  that already knows the truth for hunter  hunter this truth is the fact that  people usually aren't either good or bad  they are grey and morally highly complex  driven by desires thoughts and the  people around them gone fails to realize  this and keeps believing that everyone  is either black or white  kilowatt understands this after removing  illumi's needle and is finally able to  love himself despite his faults  [Music]  hisoka on the other hand already knows  who he is and what he wants he's not  held back by doubt or shame  now obviously just because a character  understands the truth doesn't mean he  always does the right thing what makes  flat character arcs interesting is how  they act based on their insight and so  it often makes these characters a lot  more versatile and complex as they can  use this truth to do both good or bad in  the worlds thus hisoka isn't just this  one-dimensional character as some people  like to believe which is why i love the  shower scene which might be the single  most important moment of his character  [Music]  the narrator is basically saying sit  back turn off your brain and enjoy the  [ __ ] show that is hisoka's life and  since hisoka doesn't have to go through  the same process of learning the truth  anymore as the other characters we can  see their development in comparison to  the constant that is hisoka's character  and that brings me to the main point of  this video based on all that we've  talked about so far all the fantastic  writing and the character design the  thing that truly makes hisoka a  masterpiece of storytelling  is the fact that you dear viewer are  being manipulated by hisoka as well as  am i this becomes clear in all the  controversy around him we get so much  mixed information about this man is he  good or bad a role model or the worst  type of person relatable or repulsive  all these conflicting emotions are the  true genius behind togashi's writing so  is hisoka actually good at heart but has  a hard shell or is he actually just  cruel and selfish to the core  manipulating us just like the other  characters into thinking that he has a  good side or something in between we  will probably never be able to tell we  love him for his cool manner and his  fantastic fighting skills but despise  him for his cruelty and lies and so all  we can really do is sit on the edge of  our seats whenever he shows up not  knowing if we're gonna get the carrot or  the stick togashi has created hisoka to  thrust the central moral argument of  hansa hunter into our faces human  morality is complex there is no clear  black and white so we might as well lean  back and enjoy the [ __ ] show that is the  life of hisoka moro
 

